# File: tests/features/add_public_greeting_has_hyphen_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/179-add-public-greeting-has-hyphen-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Detect a literal hyphen-minus in a completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Detect literal hyphen-minus in a completed greeting
    Given the public greeting package and valid name Mary-Jane
    When greeting_has_hyphen is called with Mary-Jane
    Then greet returns Hello, Mary-Jane and the helper returns True

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Reject absent hyphen-minus and Unicode dash lookalikes
    Given valid names Ada, Ada‐, and Ada–
    When greeting_has_hyphen is called with each valid name
    Then each completed greeting lacks literal hyphen-minus and each helper result is False

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve greet validation for invalid names
    Given invalid names empty, whitespace-only, None, and 42
    When greeting_has_hyphen is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Import and run documented helper examples
    Given the installed public package and README Library examples Mary-Jane and Ada
    When greeting_has_hyphen is imported from nmg_sdlc_smoke and called with those names
    Then the imported helper returns True and False respectively
